[list]
[*]Fixed: on a high UI scale, a stand's work-type window drew its lower half outside itself. The trigger rows and the whole work grid were missing, the window kept the space it had reserved for them, and there was no error anywhere to explain it. If you have ever opened that window and found a blank panel under the heading, this was why, and it is why ticking a work type was impossible rather than merely awkward.
[*]It depended on your screen, not your mods. What matters is display height divided by UI scale: 1920x1080 at 3x, a 1366x768 laptop at 2x, or anything windowed smaller. Below roughly 460 of those units the rows above the grid needed more room than the window had, and RimWorld's own list widget responds to that by starting a second column, which for a full-width list begins past the edge of the window. Everything from that row on was drawn where nobody could see it.
[*]The window now scrolls as a whole when it does not fit, so nothing can be pushed out of it. On a screen where it does fit, the work grid no longer sits in a scrolling panel of its own, which means the window has no clipped area in it at all. Checked at four sizes down to 480x270, the smallest RimWorld's own UI scale settings allow.
[*]Nothing about which work a stand serves has changed, and no setting moved. If the window has always looked right for you, it still does.
[/list]
